Notice on door: Open FIGGY BAR in room 2. Tonight's question:Now that you've
seen Bob Berkey's and Bob Smith's arguments for floored division do you
support floored,truncated,both ?
  
 This question elicited ho-hums and strong anti-standards sentiment. The rest
 of the FIGGY was largely occupied with discussion of the Santa Cruz/San
 Francisco quake. Forth discussion included Don Golding teaching Forth to
 sixth graders, the question of EXPECT and counted strings, more on why
 standards won't work, a whisper about RTX-2000. 
    
 Personal note: I am indebted to Kevin Appert for forwarding log notes after
                bad weather in Little Rock (snow and wind) knocked me off-line.

